{#
  The shell every page of this subsystem shares: the head, the bar at the top, the
  period, what the reading could not say, and the frame.

  It is its own shell, not `commons/base.njk`: the shared one asks for the language
  and the translation of a page of the product, and this is internal
  instrumentation, whose labels are metric names and system terms and stay in
  English like the rest of what is internal. Same reason as configurator-fe; see
  README.md.

  Blocks: `title`, `content`.
  Expected: view.page, view.navigation, view.period, view.readAt, view.metricsUrl,
            view.failures, view.truncations.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{% block title %}{{ view.page.label }} — webtools metrics{% endblock %}</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>

<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="brand">webtools <span>metrics</span></span>
    <span class="read-at">read at {{ view.readAt }} UTC</span>
  </div>
</header>

<nav class="index">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- for entry in view.navigation %}
    <a href="{{ entry.route }}{% if entry.usesPeriod and view.period %}?from={{ view.period.from }}&to={{ view.period.to }}{% endif %}"
       {% if entry.current %}class="current" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ entry.label }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</nav>

{#
  The period, in one row above everything it scopes. It is not repeated inside a
  section: two controls for the same slice are two ways for a page to disagree with
  itself.

  Nothing on it refreshes by itself. "Read again" is a link, because a picture that
  changed while it was being read would be a reading of a moment nobody asked about.
#}
{%- if view.page.usesPeriod and view.period %}
<div class="period">
  <div class="wrap">
    <form class="range" method="get" action="{{ view.page.route }}">
      <label>from <input type="date" name="from" value="{{ view.period.from }}" max="{{ view.period.today }}"></label>
      <label>to <input type="date" name="to" value="{{ view.period.to }}" max="{{ view.period.today }}"></label>
      {%- if view.chosen %}<input type="hidden" name="metric" value="{{ view.chosen }}">{% endif %}
      <button type="submit">read</button>
    </form>
    <span class="presets">
      {%- for preset in view.period.presets %}
      {%- if preset.current %}
      <span class="current">{{ preset.days }}d</span>
      {%- else %}
      <a href="{{ view.page.route }}?from={{ preset.from }}&to={{ preset.to }}{% if view.chosen %}&metric={{ view.chosen }}{% endif %}">{{ preset.days }}d</a>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </span>
    <span class="steps">
      <a href="{{ view.page.route }}?from={{ view.period.previous.from }}&to={{ view.period.previous.to }}{% if view.chosen %}&metric={{ view.chosen }}{% endif %}"
         title="the same length, one length earlier">&larr; earlier</a>
      {%- if view.period.next %}
      <a href="{{ view.page.route }}?from={{ view.period.next.from }}&to={{ view.period.next.to }}{% if view.chosen %}&metric={{ view.chosen }}{% endif %}">later &rarr;</a>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="absent">later &rarr;</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </span>
    <span class="spread">
      <span class="days">{{ view.period.from }} &rarr; {{ view.period.to }}</span>
      <span class="note">{{ view.period.days }} day{% if view.period.days != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% if not view.period.endsToday %}, not ending today{% endif %}</span>
    </span>
    <a class="again" href="?{{ 'from=' + view.period.from + '&to=' + view.period.to }}{% if view.chosen %}&metric={{ view.chosen }}{% endif %}">read again</a>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif %}

<main class="wrap">
{#
  What the reading could not say, before any figure. A reading that could not be used
  and a reading that ran out are two different things, and each of them changes what
  the numbers below mean.

  A reading that answered "there is no such thing" is not here: it is an answer, and
  the page that asked for it says so itself.
#}
{%- if view.failures.length %}
  <section class="failure">
    <h2>{{ view.failures.length }} reading{% if view.failures.length != 1 %}s{% endif %} could not be used</h2>
    <p class="note">Nothing has been put in their place.</p>
    <table class="grid">
      <thead><tr><th>reading</th><th>what happened</th><th>detail</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for failure in view.failures %}
        <tr>
          <th>{{ failure.name }}</th>
          <td><span class="outcome {{ failure.reason }}">{{ failure.reason }}</span>{% if failure.code %} <code>{{ failure.code }}</code>{% endif %}</td>
          <td class="detail">{{ failure.detail }}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
{%- endif %}

{%- if view.truncations.length %}
  <section class="warning">
    <h3>The buckets ran out before the period did</h3>
    <p>In {{ view.truncations | join(", ") }}. Those figures are of part of the period, not of the period
      (<code>limits.max_rows</code> in metrics): read a shorter one.</p>
  </section>
{%- endif %}

{% block content %}{% endblock %}

  <footer>
    <p>Read from metrics at <code>{{ view.metricsUrl }}</code>. Tokens, never money.</p>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
